[
    {
        "id": "ex38-tab",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "SITL 38 PX4 Move reposition carrier",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "PX4 twin of SITL 37 \u2014 closes #239\u2019s last acceptance box: DO_REPOSITION via mavlink-move against PX4 sysid 11, CHANGE_MODE on (the shape SITL 17 measured accepted through mavlink-command). Records the ACK result either way; if accepted, yaw 90 must turn the nose EAST (param4 radians on PX4, \u00a714).",
        "env": []
    },
    {
        "id": "ex38-comment",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "ex38-tab",
        "name": "PX4 Move carrier=reposition \u2014 measurement twin of 37",
        "info": "Flow: Arm (COMMAND_LONG) -> Takeoff 10 m (COMMAND_LONG) -> delay -> Move reposition (COMMAND_INT / DO_REPOSITION, GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT).\n\nPrerequisite: ArduCopter in GUIDED before the chain fires (harness prep ap-guided-1). CHANGE_MODE is deliberately OFF here \u2014 this measures the plain guided goto; the without-GUIDED and CHANGE_MODE cases are separate runs.\n\nWhat this run measures (\u00a714 \u2014 nothing ships as an advisory until it does):\n1. AP accepts DO_REPOSITION from Move and the COMMAND_ACK reaches output 1 with resultCode 0.\n2. param4 yaw is RADIANS on the wire. Yaw is set to 90 degrees, so a correct encode turns the vehicle EAST (pi/2 rad). The dialect and MAVSDK both say radians but that is source-read, not measured; if the vehicle ends on any other heading the conversion is wrong.\n3. Blank speed and blank radius encode the spec sentinels (-1 = vehicle default, 0 = ignored) without disturbing the goto.\n\nCompare against SITL 19, which sends the identical goto via mavlink-command."
    },
